;; SRFI 14 (char-sets): where scheme/lib/srfi/%3a14/char-sets.sls comes from (SM6)
[{:file "scheme/lib/srfi/%3a14/char-sets.sls"
  :repo "https://github.com/scheme-requests-for-implementation/srfi-14" :commit "d6e98129d1e075c03bfe4dcb30e1b5847727e26e"
  :path "srfi-14.scm" :sha256 "d1dd68b4cb6ebb49bb730c8fc7c49a0324d984a38dcb21825f30752df823ab24"
  :license "MIT Scheme license (LICENSE.md, SRFI 14)"
  :changes "Representation rewritten: the original is Latin-1 only (256-character strings); a char set is now a record of a sorted list of code point ranges, the set algebra a sweep over range lists, the standard sets computed from char-general-category on first use. The procedures keep the original's names, argument orders, optional arguments, boundary cases and descending iteration order. R6RS wrapping and define-record-type, assertion-violation for error/check-arg, rest-argument parsing for let-optionals*; surrogates excluded from char-set:full and complements. The tests (test/scheme/srfi/srfi-14.sps) are the official srfi-14-tests.scm (sha256 97943c370dd7a09857e9f6dd9f12987d857a510ef8a2d6661990f57322244ed3) in a small harness, one change: the char-set-unfold test's base is ASCII digits (char-set:digit is every Nd character here)."}]
